# Button style

Action buttons share the weather-card / app-card corner radius via `--radius-button` (aliased to `--radius-md` / 12px).

## Must do

- Use Angular Material `mat-flat-button` / `mat-unelevated-button` (primary), `mat-stroked-button` (secondary), or `mat-button` (tertiary text). Prefer `.app-btn*` utilities only when Material is not appropriate.
- Corner radius must be `var(--radius-button)` — never hardcoded px values.
- Rely on global overrides in `src/styles/material-overrides.css`. Do not re-declare `border-radius` on feature CSS unless necessary; if you must, use `var(--radius-button)`.
- Primary = filled with `--primary`; secondary = stroked; destructive = `mat-warn` + confirmation dialog.

## Must not

- Force `--radius-button` on `mat-icon-button` — icon buttons stay circular.
- Hardcode `border-radius` on action buttons (e.g. `8px`, `14px`).
- Invent a one-off button shape that diverges from weather-card rounding.

## Examples

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<button mat-flat-button color="primary" type="button">Save</button>
<button mat-stroked-button type="button">Cancel</button>

<!-- ❌ BAD — custom radius on an action button -->
<button mat-flat-button type="button" style="border-radius: 4px">Save</button>
```

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
.my-cta {
  min-height: var(--button-height);
  /* shape comes from Material + --radius-button */
}

/* ❌ BAD */
.my-cta {
  border-radius: 8px;
}
```
